---
interface Props {
  detailed?: boolean;
}

const { detailed = false } = Astro.props;
---

<figure class="pipeline">
  <ol class="rail">
    <li class="station">
      <h4>A request arrives</h4>
      <p>A Jira key, a GitHub or GitLab issue, a Slack thread, or a Sentry error.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="station">
      <h4><code>triage</code> reads the code it touches</h4>
      <p>Read-only. It picks exactly one route and drafts any reply without posting it.</p>
      <ul class="routes" aria-label="Triage routes">
        <li class="go">automate<small>small and clear: one seat builds it</small></li>
        <li class="go">spec<small>needs design before anyone builds</small></li>
        <li>clarify<small>a question goes back to the author</small></li>
        <li>park<small>not now, with the reason written down</small></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li class="station">
      <h4><code>ux-shaper</code> and <code>architect</code> write it down</h4>
      <p>
        Every screen and state first, then a spec in <code>docs/specs/</code> with one owner per slice, the contract between
        slices, and an ADR for each choice that is hard to undo.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="station gate">
      <h4>You approve the spec</h4>
      <p>Nothing is built before a person has read what will be built.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="station">
      <h4>Staff seats build in parallel</h4>
      <p>Each seat owns its files, works in its own git worktree, and clears its failure-modes checklist before it may report done.</p>
      <ul class="seats" aria-label="Example seats">
        <li>frontend</li>
        <li>backend</li>
        <li>database</li>
        <li>qa</li>
      </ul>
      <aside class="branch">
        <h5>When a seat hits a choice it may not make alone</h5>
        <p>
          Adding a dependency, breaking a shared API, inventing a design token: the seat stops and
          returns <code>needs-decision</code> with a recommendation. <code>decision-judge</code> looks for a precedent in your ADRs
          and past rulings. With one, it answers and cites it. Without one, the question comes to you, and your answer is
          recorded so the next run does not ask again.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </li>
    <li class="station">
      <h4><code>code-reviewer</code> reads the diff twice</h4>
      <p>It has no write tools, so the diff it reviewed is the diff that ships. Round one returns fix briefs; round two only reports.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="station gate">
      <h4>You review and ship</h4>
      <p><code>/code-review</code>, then <code>/ship</code> for conventional commits and the PR. No agent ever commits, pushes or merges.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  {
    detailed && (
      <figcaption>
        The ochre stations are the only places the pipeline waits. Everything between them runs without you, and everything
        that crosses one has your name on it.
      </figcaption>
    )
  }
</figure>

<style>
  .pipeline {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .rail {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    position: relative;
  }

  .rail::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.6rem;
    top: 0.8rem;
    bottom: 0.8rem;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--slate);
  }

  .station {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 2rem 2.6rem;
  }

  .station::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.2rem;
    top: 0.35rem;
    width: 0.9rem;
    height: 0.9rem;
    background: var(--plaster);
    border: 2px solid var(--slate);
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .gate::before {
    background: var(--ochre);
    border-color: var(--ochre);
    width: 1.1rem;
    height: 1.1rem;
    left: 0.1rem;
  }

  .gate h4 {
    color: var(--ochre-ink);
  }

  .station h4 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .station h4 code {
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--ai-ink);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  .station p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--sumi-soft);
  }

  .routes,
  .seats {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .routes li,
  .seats li {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .routes li {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-tile);
    color: var(--sumi-soft);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    max-width: 14rem;
  }

  .routes li.go {
    border: 1.5px solid var(--slate);
    color: var(--sumi);
  }

  .routes small {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--sumi-soft);
  }

  .seats li {
    background: var(--ai);
    color: var(--grout);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-tile);
  }

  .branch {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    background: var(--ochre-wash);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--ochre);
  }

  .branch h5 {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .branch p {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--sumi);
  }

  figcaption {
    color: var(--sumi-soft);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
</style>
